  "visualAssessment": {
    "findings": [
      "V7 linear-to-sRGB conversion raises base-colour RGB means while preserving alpha exactly; normals and per-LOD geometry content hashes are unchanged. No opaque base-colour channel clips to byte 255 in either changed texture.",
      "Compared with v6 in same browser camera/lighting, 3-instance LOD0/LOD1 renders visibly brighten; overall foliage reads clearer green. It is still notably dark on the back-lit side when the sun is behind the canopy, including with cast shadows disabled, so shadow-map toggling alone does not remove directional shading contrast.",
      "The separate fixed-light harness confirms the base-color and normal maps load as sRGB/material inputs with foliage alphaTest .5 and double-sided rendering. Its no-normal-map variant remains directionally contrasted; the neutral-map variant removes alpha cutout and is only a diagnostic."
    ],
    "visualAcceptance": "Open. This checks one fixed studio fixture and two authored LOD files, not species variations or gameplay/world lighting."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "RTX 5090 desktop WebGL only; no midrange device or XR.",
    "The lab is not the in-game forest and its draw/triangle totals are fixture measurements, not projected runtime gains.",
    "Static images cannot validate wind appearance, bark seam frequency along all branches, long-distance LOD transition or seasonal color."
  ]
